    UI strings for tamp.findings.

    Strings belong here, never hard-coded in markup. Embedded markup inside a
    localized string goes through a composed fragment with NUMBERED
    PLACEHOLDERS so translators receive {0}/{1} rather than tags — the Blazor
    equivalent of the React <Trans> rule. Do not concatenate localized
    fragments: word order differs between languages and concatenation makes a
    sentence untranslatable.

    Design for ~40% expansion and verify against the pseudo-locale
    (?culture=qps-ploc). Several layouts are CSS grids with fixed columns, and
    those columns are minimums chosen for English.
  -->
